  "title": "Another so-called kingdom rises against the Emperor's rule, and this time Ṭulayṭula itself leads it. The city drives out its governor and damages the madrasa built in its heart, and the revolt sweeps 58 towns into a Kingdom of Toledo: the Middle March and La Mancha, the hills of Extremadura, and even Mursiyya, Jayyān, Ubbadha and Bayyāsa in the old lands. It raises 5,900 men against the Emperor's 3,700 regulars",
